  "worked_solution": "First, we move the constant term to the right-hand side and complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}^{2}+14b+14 & =0 \\\\ {b}^{2}+14b & =-14 \\\\ {b}^{2}+2\\cdot 7\\cdot b & =-14 \\\\ {b}^{2}+2\\cdot 7\\cdot b+{7}^{2}-{7}^{2} & =-14 \\\\ (b+7{)}^{2}-49 & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we isolate the perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(b+7{)}^{2}-49 & =-14 \\\\ (b+7{)}^{2} & =35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p=7,$ $q=35$ and $p+q=42.$",
